>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_typedef`

``` hol4
Refute.register_typedef :
  {ty : hol_type,
   abs : term,
   rep : term,
   absrep_thms : thm list} -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Registers an existing type definition with the model finder.

`ty` is the abstract type, whose operator parameters must be distinct
type variables; the representation type may not introduce further type
variables.  `abs` and `rep` must be existing constants with mutually
opposite abstract and representation types.  `absrep_thms` is either
the standard hypothesis-free conjunction of the Abs/Rep bijection
properties as a singleton list, or its two conjuncts
`!a. abs (rep a) = a` and `!r. P r = (rep (abs r) = r)` as separate
theorems in either order; the two forms register identically.  Refute
recovers the representation predicate and verifies it against the
type's `<tyop>_TY_DEF` theorem.

Registrations are session-local; a valid later registration replaces
the same typedef operator.  The model finder also harvests standard
typedef metadata lazily.

### Failure

Fails for malformed type parameters, missing or mismatched
type-definition metadata, nonconstant or ill-typed Abs/Rep terms,
theorem hypotheses or an unsupported theorem shape, an `absrep_thms`
list that is not one or two theorems long, two theorems that are the
same bijection half or name different Abs/Rep constants, or an
incompatible datatype, codatatype, quotient, or fraction
classification.

### See also

[`Refute.register_quotient`](#Refute.register_quotient),
[`Refute.register_codatatype`](#Refute.register_codatatype),
[`Refute.register_frac_type`](#Refute.register_frac_type),
[`Refute.harvest_registrations`](#Refute.harvest_registrations),
[`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute)

Typedef encoding is described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
